#!/usr/bin/env bash
#MISE description="Fill Tuist cache"
set -euo pipefail

# No flags, deliberately. Every argument here has to match what a plain `tuist generate` asks for,
# because the hash it uploads under is the hash that generate looks up — warm it under anything
# else and the cache fills with entries nobody ever finds.
#
# `--cache-profile` is not passed: the profile lives in Tuist.swift, which `tuist generate` reads
# too. It is `only-external` there — warming this repository's own modules as well was tried and
# reverted, because ApiInterface's URL.projectRoot bakes in a compile-time #filePath. Tuist.swift
# says why.
# `--configuration Debug` is simply gone: it changed the hash even though Debug is already the
# default configuration, so passing it turned all 72 external targets into misses.
#
# Warming uploads to the remote cache by default, so this is also what makes the cache shared rather
# than local to whichever machine happened to run it. That needs the server, which is why the step
# is wrapped in `fnox exec -P ci` — unauthenticated, `tuist cache` fails rather than quietly warming
# nothing.
tuist cache
